{"hash": "bf375e0a2990b041", "text": "Aaron, who made this course, once wrote Python in Notepad and saved it as dot T X T. Today an agent would do all of that for him. Five years ago, AI in coding meant autocomplete. You ran the program, read the error, searched for it, and fixed it yourself. In 2022, you could paste the error into a chat, and paste the fix back. Since 2025, the agent runs the code, reads its own error, fixes it, and runs it again until the check passes. Aaron hasn't had to debug an error himself since he started using Claude Code. Writing and debugging code by hand is quickly becoming the exception. Google says about three quarters of its new code is now written by AI. Anthropic says most of its own is. Notice why crashes went first: a crash is something a machine can check. Andrej Karpathy calls the careful version agentic engineering: you direct, and you oversee.", "alignment": {"characters": ["A", "a", "r", "o", "n", ",", " ", "w", "h", "o", " ", "m", "a", "d", "e", " ", "t", "h", "i", "s", " ", "c", "o", "u", "r", "s", "e", ",", " ", "o", "n", "c", "e", " ", "w", "r", "o", "t", "e", " ", "P", "y", "t", "h", "o", "n", " ", "i", "n", " ", "N", "o", "t", "e", "p", "a", "d", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "s", "a", "v", "e", "d", " ", "i", "t", " ", "a", "s", " ", "d", "o", "t", " ", "T", " ", "X", " ", "T", ".", " ", "T", "o", "d", "a", "y", " ", "a", "n", " ", "a", "g", "e", "n", "t", " ", "w", "o", "u", "l", "d", " ", "d", "o", " ", "a", "l", "l", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "f", "o", "r", " ", "h", "i", "m", ".", " ", "F", "i", "v", "e", " ", "y", "e", "a", "r", "s", " ", "a", "g", "o", ",", " ", "A", "I", " ", "i", "n", " ", "c", "o", "d", "i", "n", "g", " ", "m", "e", "a", "n", "t", " ", "a", "u", "t", "o", "c", "o", "m", "p", "l", "e", "t", "e", ".", " ", "Y", "o", "u", " ", "r", "a", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "p", "r", "o", "g", "r", "a", "m", ",", " ", "r", "e", "a", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "e", "r", "r", "o", "r", ","